# Written by PanelAlpha. Group Office ships no .htaccess of its own.
#
# The document root is this directory -- `app_root: www` makes ~/project/www
# the container's /app and PhpDocroot then answers PA_DOCROOT=/app -- and
# upstream's layout puts rather more than the front controller in it. Every
# rule below was checked against a real deploy: each of these answered an
# unauthenticated request, and none is reachable through index.php, so denying
# them costs the application nothing.
#
# The generated vhost already denies dotfiles and anything named `panelalpha-*`
# or `docker-compose.ya?ml` (resources/deploy/templates/apache-vhost.stub), so
# panelalpha-install.php, panelalpha-setup.sh, .panelalpha/ and
# .panelalpha-admin-password need no rule here. This file covers what upstream
# put here.
#
# RedirectMatch rather than <Directory>: <Directory> is a server-config
# container and Apache refuses to start reading one from an .htaccess. A real
# `Require all denied` for install/ is in files/www/install/.htaccess, which is
# where a directory container can be expressed; these are the outer belt.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# install/ -- the whole tree.
#
# This is the important one. It is an unauthenticated wizard with three
# separate holes, and unlike most web installers it does not stop being
# reachable once the application is installed:
#
#   configfile.php  rewrites ../config.php from POST fields -- database host,
#                   name, user, password and the data paths -- with no
#                   authentication (configfile.php:103-112). A stranger can
#                   point a fresh deploy at a database they control, and the
#                   GET form discloses the current host, name and user
#                   (configfile.php:76-80).
#   install.php     creates the System Administrator from POST
#                   (install.php:71-85). First visitor wins.
#   upgrade.php     runs schema migrations. For the life of the installation,
#                   not only before it is installed: index.php -> test.php ->
#                   configfile.php -> install.php, and install.php redirects
#                   straight to upgrade.php as soon as the database is
#                   non-empty (install.php:52-55).
#   gotest.php      a full system report, down to the loaded extensions.
#   clearcache.php  rebuilds the cache on request. Only a denial of service,
#                   but free to deny: this recipe clears the cache from the CLI.
#
# Everything this directory does is done by panelalpha-install.php on the
# install and upgrade stages instead, before Apache binds. index.php's error
# handler redirects here when it cannot boot, which on a working deploy does
# not happen and on a broken one should be a 404 rather than an open wizard.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/install(/|$)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# vendor/ -- Composer's tree.
#
# Nothing in Group Office links to an asset under vendor/ (checked: no URL
# built in views/ or go/core/webclient/ resolves there), and it is thirty-odd
# libraries' worth of examples, tests and tools -- including tcpdf's, whose own
# tools/ directory ships an .htaccess saying exactly this.
#
# A rule here rather than a vendor/.htaccess because vendor/ does not exist
# when this file is written: the recipe's files/ are copied in right after the
# clone and `composer install` runs later, on the host.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/vendor(/|$)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Command-line entry points that happen to sit in the document root.
#
# cli.php, cron.php and groupofficecli.php are argv-driven scripts; `groupoffice`
# is a shell wrapper Apache would serve as plain text. None is reachable
# through index.php and none has any business answering a request. Group
# Office's cron runs from the account's own scheduler, not over HTTP.
<FilesMatch "^(?:cli|cron|groupofficecli)\.php$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
<Files "groupoffice">
    Require all denied
</Files>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# config.php.
#
# It holds no literal secret -- this recipe writes it as a list of getenv()
# calls -- and Apache executes .php rather than disclosing it. Denied anyway,
# because the one thing making that true is a mod_php that is working, and the
# file naming the account's database is not worth betting on that.
<FilesMatch "^config\.php(?:\.example)?$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependency and build manifests. Information disclosure only -- the exact
# version of every library in the tree, which is a shopping list for anyone
# matching advisories against the site.
<FilesMatch "^(?:composer|package|package-lock)\.(?:json|lock)$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
<Files "composer.lock">
    Require all denied
</Files>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# display_errors and friends.
#
# Belt and braces for files/www/.panelalpha/php/zz-groupoffice.ini: the base
# image loads no php.ini at all (#185), so display_errors is on and a single
# notice is rendered into the page for every visitor -- with absolute paths in
# it, as measured on this application before the ini existed. PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR
# is the real fix and reaches the CLI too; this covers the Apache side if that
# environment variable is ever lost. `php_flag` is mod_php's, and mod_php is
# what the base image runs (panelalpha-serve.sh execs apache2-foreground).
<IfModule php_module>
php_flag display_errors Off
php_flag log_errors On
</IfModule>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Z-Push's command-line tools, which ship inside the document root.
#
# The activesync module vendors Z-Push as a git submodule -- which the engine
# fetches after the clone -- and Z-Push ships its administration and migration
# scripts as ordinary .php files under src/ and tools/. Found by asking the
# tree rather than by guessing: every .php under the document root whose first
# line is a `#!` shebang is one of these, plus cli.php, cron.php and
# groupofficecli.php, which are denied above.
#
# Measured on a real deploy: `GET /modules/z-push/z-push-admin.php` answered
# 200 and wrote its shebang line into the response before failing on a constant
# it only has under the CLI. Nothing here is reachable through the application
# and none of it has any business answering a request.
#
# Z-Push/src/index.php is NOT denied: that one is the ActiveSync endpoint a
# phone talks to, and it is the reason the submodule is here at all.
<FilesMatch "^(?:z-push-admin|z-push-top|wbxml|checkshares|listfolders|gab-sync|gab2contacts|list-shared-folders|migrate-2\.0\.x-2\.1\.0|migrate-filestates-to-db)\.php$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Z-Push's tools/ and config trees wholesale, for anything added upstream later
# that this list does not name. config.php there holds an ActiveSync backend
# configuration, not the account's database credentials, but it is still not a
# page.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/go/modules/community/activesync/Z-Push/(?:tools|config)(/|$)
